Z||000000||penetrator||07-17-2000||07:35 AM||||My car (GT V6-86) have started to sound really strange when have been driving about 160 kilometers, there is some rattling noise in the 1st-3rd gear. Even when then clutch is engaded and when im down shifting from the 4th gear to 3rd it sounds like something is loose in the gearbox. And when im standing still and putting in the 1st gear and just when the car is starting to drag the sounds come again? And when im letting the car stand for about 5 hours and let it get cold, the noise is gone? What can it be? Im really worried. And its only starting when i have been driving a lng ride.<P>HELP!||||reg||1
Z||000001||loafer87gt||07-17-2000||11:45 AM||||If you go to your GM dealership and have them check through the service bulletins you will find find that this is a common problem with the 5-spd tranny in the V6's. From what I gathered, the gears inside the transmission start to wear down and you get a sort of tumbling/rattling noise in the tranny. My car started to this last summer, but the tranny still works fine, and I haven't had any problems with it. One thing that the GM service bulletin reccomends is using the GM synchromesh transmission fluid to quiet things down. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||penetrator||07-18-2000||07:26 AM||||okey, i'll will try that other fluid you talked about, now i got the GM standard fluid for manual transmissions.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
